course: dictionary
lesson: 14550
title: Petroleum: the oil under our feet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Petroleum is a noun. Context helps you work out its meaning. «Workers pumped petroleum up from deep under the sea.» Pumped and deep under the sea are the clues: it is something taken out of the ground, and it flows like a liquid.
explain: Look at the next example: «Many bags, toys and bottles are made from petroleum.» Made from tells you petroleum is a raw material, something other things are built out of. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Many bags are made from thick dark oil" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: The same word can have a second meaning: «Mum rubbed petroleum jelly on her dry, chapped lips.» The word jelly is a clue. Petroleum jelly is a soft, greasy substance made from oil, not a sweet dessert. Always check the words around the new word before you decide what it means.
fact: Petroleum means crude oil: a thick, dark liquid found deep underground.
fact: Petroleum is used to make petrol, diesel, plastics and many other things.
fact: Petroleum is a fossil fuel, formed from tiny sea creatures over millions of years.
fact: Petroleum is non-renewable: once it is used up, it cannot be replaced quickly. Burning it adds carbon dioxide to the air.
fact: Petroleum jelly is a soft, greasy substance made from oil, used on dry skin.
exercise: «Workers pumped petroleum up from deep under the sea.» What does petroleum mean? | Sea water mixed with sand | Hard grey rock | A type of fish | *Crude oil, a thick dark liquid from underground
exercise: «Many bags, toys and bottles are made from petroleum.» What is petroleum used for here? | Growing vegetables | *Making plastics and other things | Cooking soup | Lighting candles only
exercise: «Mum rubbed petroleum jelly on her dry, chapped lips.» What is petroleum jelly used for? | To keep sweets fresh | To make bread rise | *To soften dry skin | To clean the windows
test: Petroleum is non-renewable. What does that mean? | It can be replaced quickly | *It cannot be replaced quickly once it is used up | It is made from wood | It is found in every garden
test: What is petroleum formed from? | *Tiny sea creatures over millions of years | Trees that fell in the forest | Rocks and sand | Fresh rain water
exam: Which of these is made from petroleum? | *Petrol | Wool | Glass | Cotton
